# dlt boundaries in DET

dlt is extraction tooling only. DET owns validation, naming, meta, landing, state,
and any reshaping of wire payloads into bronze.

## Allowed

- `@dlt.resource` / `DltResource` as an iterator when a source chooses to use it
- `dlt.sources.helpers.requests` for HTTP retries (prefer plain `requests` when
  retries/hangs are a problem — see NOAA)
- `dlt.sources.helpers.rest_client` (`RESTClient`, paginators, auth)

## Forbidden

- `dlt.pipeline(...)` / `pipeline.run(...)` for bronze or any landed data
- Letting dlt manage load/pipeline state (`_dlt_loads`, `_dlt_pipeline_state`,
  `_dlt_version`, `_dlt_id`, `_dlt_load_id`)
- Letting dlt's normalizer unnest nested fields or rename `__*` meta columns
- Using dlt destinations as the bronze writer

Source bytes land under `raw/.../data/`; DET sidecars under `raw/.../meta/`.
Bronze lands through DET-owned writers (e.g. `write_jsonl_partition`). Rebuilds
use `det migrate` from raw data files, not from a bronze payload column.
